{"id":"20260826T002516.966251028Z-090727b5","time":"2026-08-26T00:25:16.966251028Z","session_id":"session-20260826T001911.176283452Z","task_id":"task-1787703551176526418","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  internal/setup does not notice candidate worktrees left behind by earlier runs, so a repository accumulates abandoned checkouts beside it that nothing reports.\n\nInspect must include a Check named \"candidate worktrees\" in its Report. A repository with no leftovers reports OK. A leftover directory that is EMPTY is reported and carries a Repair that removes it. A leftover directory HOLDING FILES is reported and is never deleted automatically -- unfinished work is not litter -- and the check says where it is so a person can decide. A worktree git still considers live is not abandoned.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] setup.Inspect constructs the readiness Report from an ordered list of checks and receives the canonical repository root through Options.RepoRoot. (internal/setup/checks.go:Inspect and Options) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Report.Ready blocks only on Broken checks, while Degraded checks may carry Repair callbacks that setup.Apply executes. (internal/setup/setup.go:Report.Ready, Report.Repairable, and Apply) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The CLI renders the report before repair, runs repairs only when --apply is supplied, and then re-inspects instead of assuming success. (cmd/sensei-code/setup.go:runSetup) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Candidate worktrees are placed under a sibling directory named from the repository basename, and Git worktree commands create and remove registered candidates. (internal/gitx/git.go:Repo.WorktreePath, CreateWorktree, and RemoveWorktree) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Repository intent requires interrupted candidates to be retained so unfinished work can be resumed or inspected. (docs/intent/sensei_code.candidates_are_isolated.yaml) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei holds an active critical invariant that candidate removal must be decided and its evidence must outlive removal. (candidate disposition lifecycle) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] The scoped preflight reports local blast radius with no approval gate, but low-confidence thin coverage because the proposed test file is not indexed. (internal/setup/checks.go and internal/setup/checks_test.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] This checkout currently has no test file in internal/setup, so the regression suite will be introduced as internal/setup/checks_test.go. (internal/setup test coverage) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
